4. Assess real demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) whether the following 1-3 months show a sharp drop (suggesting channel stuffing), (b) whether the 24-month trend before the spike was flat or growing (suggesting real demand), (c) the return rate level. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/anomaly_assessment.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded data: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 anomalies with region, product line, month, sales volume, 24-month mean, ratio, return rate; (3) every key number must carry an inline source annotation in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is more likely real demand or channel stuffing, with reasoning; (5) all data sourced exclusively from the local CSV, no web data. → code_agent
